  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#4879\", \"PowerToys#32406\", \"PowerToys#33566\"], \"answer\": \"This feature request has been filed before. PowerToys#4879 is the main thread, and later duplicates such as #33566 were closed in its favor. PowerToys has no built-in configurable hotkey to turn Keyboard Manager on or off. Add your thumbs-up to #4879 to show demand. Two workarounds from that thread may help. First, use a PowerShell script that stops or starts the PowerToys.KeyboardManagerEngine process. Bind it to a hotkey through a desktop shortcut with a shortcut key, or through AutoHotkey. Second, one commenter suggested adding a Keyboard Manager on/off toggle to the PowerToys Run plugin. I haven't confirmed that it exists. With the script, the PowerToys settings page may not show the correct on/off state.\"}",
